# What the DEV server keeps: never uploaded, never deleted there.
#
# One path per line, from the project root; * matches within a folder. The
# upload mirrors the project with --delete, so anything not listed here that
# the upload does not carry is removed from the server. cache/, logs/ and data/
# are written by the running application, and a deployment that swept them
# would wipe compiled templates, the day's log and the database with every
# stored request.
#
# runtime.local.php and .well-known/ are always kept, listed or not.
# runtime.dev.php can never be kept back: the DEV deployment writes it and
# must upload it.
#
# The repository's own material — .git/, .github/, .agent/, .claude/,
# .codex/, every Markdown file, docs/, LLM.txt, captures/,
# tests/ — is never deployed. The workflow leaves it out and fails if it is
# there; it does not need listing.
#
# DEV keeps __dev/ (the probe, diagnostics and migrator). Only the production
# package strips it — see .deployignore.production.

runtime.local.php
runtime.local.example.php
cache
logs
data
